ic) Utilization-based interest rate curves per asset (v2); simplified rate model with base/borrow asset separation (v3) Governance-set stability fees per vault type (effectively interest rates) Utilization-based IR model (Aave v3 lineage) + custom DAI/sDAI strategies in Spark context (Medium) Market-selected Interest Rate Models (IRMs); IRMs/LLTVs are constrained by governance whitelists (docs.morpho.org)": "Redemption Rate / Redemption Price mechanism (control-theory/PID-style policy) drives target price dynamics; not a utilization-based money market rate (Reflexer)", "Isolation of Risk Risk primarily at market/reserve parameter level (not isolated per-user); isolation features exist in newer versions/markets but not “isolated pools” by default Moderate isolation: v3 introduces asset isolation via a single base asset with segmented collateral; v2 uses shared pools High isolation at vault-type level; each collateral type has independent parameters Shared pool risk by asset/reserve parameters (not per-market isolation like Morpho Blue) High isolation: each market is isolated and immutable by design (docs.morpho.org)": "System-level shared risk (single collateral type, shared liquidation + auction plumbing), rather than isolated pools (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Launch Year 2020 (v1 Ethereum mainnet) (aave.com) 2018 (v2 on Ethereum) 2017 (Single-Collateral DAI; Multi-Collateral DAI in 2019) 2023 (public launch May 9, 2023) (X (formerly Twitter)) 2023 (Morpho Blue introduced Oct 2023) (morpho.org)": "2021-02-17 (RAI mainnet launch) (Medium)", "Lending Model Pooled liquidity markets (multi-asset) Pooled liquidity markets (v2); single-collateral base with isolated borrow assets (v3/Comet) CDP / Vault-based collateralized lending Pooled liquidity markets (Aave v3-derived money market) (Spark Docs) Permissionless, isolated lending markets (1 collateral + 1 loan asset per market) (docs.morpho.org)": "CDP / SAFE-based borrowing (Maker-style architecture via GEB framework) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Liquidation Mechanism Onchain liquidations triggered when Health Factor < 1; liquidators repay debt for collateral + bonus (bonus/thresholds per asset, governance/risk-managed) (aave.com) Onchain liquidations when collateral value breaches borrow limits; liquidators repay debt for collateral at protocol-defined incentives Onchain liquidation via auctions (debt, collateral, surplus); keeper participation required Health Factor-based liquidations (HF < 1), onchain seizure/repay mechanics (Spark Docs) Standard liquidation when LTV exceeds LLTV; liquidators repay debt and seize collateral at discount (protocol-enforced) (docs.morpho.org)": "LiquidationEngine → CollateralAuctionHouse: unsafe SAFEs can be liquidated and collateral is auctioned to cover debt; keepers participate in auctions (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Maintaining Organization Aave DAO (governance) + Aave Labs (major dev & interface/operator tooling) (aave.com) Compound DAO (governance) with historical development by Compound Labs MakerDAO (DAO-governed protocol) with core units / contributors maintaining modules Spark Governance (SPK) operating via the Spark Agent in the Sky Atlas (Sky ecosystem) (Spark Docs) Morpho Governance (MORPHO token); governance whitelists IRMs/LLTVs and can activate fee switch (docs.morpho.org)": "Reflexer protocol community + FLX (“ungovernance”) holders with a stated goal of governance minimization over time (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Oracle Dependencies Primarily Chainlink price feeds with protocol risk controls (market-config dependent) Chainlink price feeds (primary), with protocol-defined fallbacks/guards Decentralized Oracle Network (Maker Oracles) with Chainlink integrations and redundancy Oracle-driven risk system; Spark has integrated oracle providers (e.g., RedStone) for lending markets (RedStone blog) Oracle per market; Morpho established an oracle wrapper for Chainlink feeds to support initial markets (morpho.org)": "Oracle stack includes OracleRelayer + OSM feeding safety and liquidation prices into core system logic (price + redemption price adjustments) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Parameter Control Governance-gated risk parameters + emergency controls (typical DeFi risk-admin pattern) Governance-gated parameters; admin/guardian controls for emergencies (especially during upgrades) Fully governance-controlled parameters; emergency shutdown and circuit breakers exist Parameter updates controlled through governance actions on the Spark Agent (risk, budgets, onboarding, deployments) (Spark Docs) Governance whitelists key risk parameters (LLTVs, IRMs) and can toggle fee switch (capped) (docs.morpho.org)": "Governance minimization guide documents which modules can be “ungoverned” vs where governance remains (e.g., oracle-related components / saviours) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Practitioner Validation Check YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced by contracts (HF<1) (aave.com) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced by contracts • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced via protocol auctions • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced (HF<1) (Spark Docs) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced (LTV>LLTV) (docs.morpho.org) • YES positions unwindable programmatically": "YES creates credit onchain (SAFE → mint RAI) (Reflexer) • YES liquidation enforced (LiquidationEngine → auctions) (docs.reflexer.finance) • YES unwindable programmatically (repay debt, withdraw collateral; liquidations auction collateral) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Practitioner’s Note Research focus: liquidation mechanics (health factor dynamics), collateral mix concentration, oracle coverage/fallbacks, and governance latency during fast markets. Also track version/market fragmentation (v1 frozen vs v3 active) when analyzing risk. (messari.io) Research focus: differences between v2 and v3 risk profiles; base-asset concentration in v3; liquidation throughput under stress; governance response speed during incidents. Research focus: auction efficiency during stress, oracle latency, RWA exposure and offchain enforcement risk, governance concentration, and emergency shutdown assumptions. Watchpoints: Aave v3 fork deltas (custom DAI/sDAI logic), oracle stack and feed coverage, asset-list governance, and liquidation throughput under stablecoin stress. Also note Spark’s bug bounty posture. (Spark Docs) Watchpoints: oracle selection/config is a first-order risk surface (market-by-market). Validate LLTV choice, oracle robustness, and liquidation liquidity for collateral. Review post-mortems for oracle manipulation and operational incidents. (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Watchpoints: (1) keeper participation and auction efficiency under fast ETH moves, (2) oracle/relayer correctness (safety vs liquidation price paths), (3) redemption rate regime shifts (impact on leverage incentives), (4) governance-minimization stage and any remaining admin surfaces. (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Primary Role in DeFi Base credit + leverage layer for Ethereum DeFi Base credit layer and leverage primitive for Ethereum DeFi Stablecoin issuance + base credit layer for DeFi DAI-centered credit & liquidity venue; major stablecoin + ETH collateral borrowing/supply rails inside Sky ecosystem (Blockworks) Base lending primitive for permissionless risk markets; “lending infrastructure” others build vaults/allocators on top of": "Governance-minimized, ETH-backed stable-credit primitive (non-fiat-pegged “reflex index”) used as collateral and settlement asset in DeFi (Reflexer)", "Protocol Status Active (v3 widely used; v1 largely frozen) (messari.io) Active (v3 “Comet” is primary; v2 largely deprecated/frozen for growth) Active (DAI issuance core to Ethereum DeFi) Active Active": "Active (RAI system live; governance minimization roadmap documented) (Reflexer)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending; collateralized credit issuance; onchain interest rate mechanics; liquidation + solvency enforced by protocol logic. (aave.com) Meets criteria: issues credit onchain against collateral; defines interest rates, liquidation logic, and solvency rules fully in smart contracts. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing; collateralized credit issuance; explicit liquidation and solvency logic; interest (stability fees) set and enforced onchain. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending, collateralized credit issuance, onchain interest + liquidation + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Meets criteria: onchain borrowing, collateralized credit issuance (RAI), protocol-defined solvency + liquidation (LiquidationEngine + auctions), and onchain monetary policy (redemption rate/price). (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "Medium (important conceptually; smaller systemic footprint than DAI/USDC rails, but can be critical in niche strategies) (CoinGecko)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "ETH liquidity; oracle reliability; keeper/auction participation; RAI secondary market liquidity (docs.reflexer.finance)"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb),
  ('sushiswap', 'SushiSwap', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://www.sushi.com', ARRAY['Pool-based swaps executed fully onchain']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A general-purpose AMM offering permissionless token swaps and liquidity provision, with broad asset coverage and strong long-tail liquidity.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Uniform liquidity (v2-style pools)", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Constant Product AMM (Uniswap v2-style)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "Medium LP concentration risk; Medium dependency on incentives for liquidity depth", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-controlled fee splits (LP vs protocol)", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO token governance (SUSHI)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Governance and treasury stress events (2021–2022); no core AMM insolvency events", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Yield strategies, DAO treasury swaps, long-tail asset liquidity", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2020", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "High (AMM MEV exposure similar to Uniswap v2)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Sushi DAO (governance) with Sushi core contributors maintaining protocol", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs 